--- body ---
## Context

Author request, 2026-10-29, refined three times the same day:

1. Not a one-off trim of `skills/harness-doctor/` (round 1: `3dc7ef05`) but a
   **routine checkup** offered at every visit.
2. Think **KPIs**, starting with time per ticket. The monitoring already stores
   what a quick pulse check and basic follow-up need: the checkup reads, it adds
   no instrumentation.
3. The figures go into a **long-lived, project-specific health journal** in
   JSON, to plot curves over time, not just a comparison with the last visit.
   JSON because the KPI set will change.
4. **Costs: only real billed spend.** Most cost figures (token counts times a
   price list, subscription sessions) are estimates, mostly imaginary. The only
   cost worth monitoring is what API keys are actually billed.

Survey at respecification: no store holds billed spend today.
`gaze_seat.billed_provider` routes a seat to its billing provider; it records no
amount. Billed cost is therefore the one KPI read from outside the harness: the
provider's own account of what the key was charged.

The checkup measures and records; whether to cut, and what, is the
weight-watch discussion with the author that follows, not part of this ticket.

Existing readers to reuse, not duplicate:

- Time per ticket: `scripts/slow_tickets.py` defines solve time once (sum of
  the `duration:` lines gaze, verify-gate and merge post on the PR; else PR
  open-to-merge, an upper bound; else unknown). It reads a fixed 24 h window.
- Review outcome: REROLL / ESCALATE verdicts (`scripts/trace-pr-join.py`,
  review notes).
- Main health: `idh/after-merge.log`, `idh/main-journal.jsonl` under the git
  common dir.
- Throughput and backlog: ticket `Created:` / `Closed:` headers.
- Size and timings: `scripts/skill_text_lint.py` (body length, long blocks),
  `scripts/gaze_wall_time.py`, `scripts/trace-wall-time.py`.

## Intent

One command, offered at the start of every harness-doctor visit, measures the
project and appends one record to its health journal; a second mode plots any
metric's series over time.

**KPIs (pulse)**, over the window since the previous record:

- Time per ticket: median and p90 solve time; counts recorded, derived, unknown.
- Throughput: tickets closed, opened, net backlog change.
- First-pass quality: share of PRs merged without REROLL or ESCALATE; red
  after-merge runs on main.
- Main timings: gaze wall time, test gate, session start, where traces exist.
- Billed cost: spend charged to each API key the harness uses (OpenRouter,
  Anthropic API, OpenAI API), over the window, per provider and total.

**Vital signs (weight)**:

- Length: lines of each `skills/*/SKILL.md`, its references, the resident rules,
  each script under `scripts/`; totals.
- Complexity: per script, functions and branch nodes counted with the stdlib
  `ast` module (no new dependency); per skill, steps, table rows and
  cross-references.

## Decisions

- **Journal**: `health/journal.jsonl` at the project root, committed,
  append-only, one JSON object per checkup. Outside `memory/`, so hoard never
  prunes it. Each record carries `schema`, `ts`, `host`, `commit`, `window`, and
  a flat `metrics` object of `name -> {value, unit, source}`. Readers tolerate
  unknown and missing names, so KPIs can be added, renamed (old series kept) or
  retired without migration.
- **Gaps**: a metric whose source is missing or unreadable is written with
  `value: null` and a `gap` reason, never 0 and never omitted silently.
- **Window**: `slow_tickets.py` gains a `--since` option (default unchanged)
  so the checkup covers the time since the previous record.
- **Plot**: `--plot <metric>[,<metric>...]` renders the series from the
  journal to a PNG; only this mode imports matplotlib.
- **Billed cost only**: read from each provider's billing or usage endpoint
  with the key the harness already holds, where the endpoint exists for that
  key; a provider that exposes none to that key is a `gap`. Never a token-based
  estimate, never subscription usage. Keys are never printed or written to the
  journal; record the provider name, not the key.
- The terminal report shows each figure beside the previous record and flags
  the biggest movers; the curves answer the longer view.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The harness-doctor visit menu offers the checkup at every visit; one command runs it and appends one record to `health/journal.jsonl`
- [ ] A record covers the KPIs (time per ticket, throughput, first-pass quality, main timings) and the vital signs (length, complexity), per the record shape above
- [ ] Billed cost per provider comes from the provider's own record or is a `gap`; no estimated figure appears
- [ ] A missing source yields `value: null` with a `gap` reason; a test feeds one missing source and checks it
- [ ] A reader test loads a journal whose records differ in metric names and plots a series spanning them
- [ ] `slow_tickets.py --since` covers a chosen window; its default output is unchanged
- [ ] A first run on origin/main is committed as the journal's first record and shown in the PR
- [ ] Cost of the run stated in the menu row (wall seconds measured, no model usage)
- [ ] The harness gate passes

## Plan (raid 94edd2)

Actions: (1) `scripts/slow_tickets.py`: split a `collect(root, since)` returning every
closed ticket with solve time and source; `main()` stays a thin wrapper, `--since`
added, default output unchanged (regression test). (2) `scripts/health_checkup.py`,
stdlib: one function per metric group (tickets, quality, main, timings, size,
complexity, billed cost), each returning `{name: {value, unit, source}}` and turning an
exception into `value: null` plus `gap`; record builder (`schema`, `ts`, `host`,
`commit`, `window`); append; table against the previous record with the top 3 movers
by relative change; `--plot` imports matplotlib inside the function. Hyphenated readers
load by `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location`; no logic copied. Percentiles by
`statistics.quantiles`. (3) Tests. (4) Menu row in skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md (150
line cap, 122 now) and a short metrics note in a reference. (5) First run on
origin/main, record committed, shown in the PR.

Readings fixed here: the first record's window is the last 7 days; a KPI counts as
covered when its name is present, possibly `null` with `gap`. First-pass quality reads
verdicts from `refs/notes/review` (trace-pr-join needs a census CSV a cold run lacks).
Main health parses `pass:` / `fail:` lines of `idh/after-merge.log`.

Billed cost: OpenRouter `GET /api/v1/key` returns the key's cumulative usage in USD;
journal the cumulative figure and derive the window at read time (first record: gap
for the window). Key read as `scripts/pi-openrouter` reads it, never printed. Anthropic
and OpenAI cost endpoints need admin keys: gap unless one is held. The fetcher is
injectable for tests; a test asserts no key string appears in a record.

First test: a journal of three records with differing metric names (one `null` plus
`gap`); `read_series` spans all three with `None` at the gap and tolerates unknown
names; a record built with one source raising has `value: null` and a non-empty `gap`.

Estimated wall time 30 to 90 s (the `gh` reads of slow_tickets dominate, 18.6 s
measured for its 24 h window); measure and state in the menu row.

## Feasibility (raid 94edd2): BLOCK, resolved

- matplotlib is undeclared; a lazy import does not exempt it
  (tests/test_deps_declared.py). Decision: declare it in the dev dependency group of
  pyproject.toml and regenerate uv.lock.
- Two OpenRouter keys (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY_PI`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY_IDH`, see
  skills/route/routes.json): query `/api/v1/key` once per key, one metric per key env
  name, never the value; read keys with `scripts/keystore.py` (`keystore_value`), not a
  copy of pi-openrouter's grep.
- `slow_tickets.py` keeps its positional ticket-root argument (lair calls it bare);
  `--since` is additive.
- Window capped at 30 days, stated in the menu row with the measured wall time.
- `.gitattributes`: `health/journal.jsonl merge=union`, so visits on parallel branches
  append without conflict.
- The script roots at `IDH_ROOT` (harness-doctor is harness-only); no `/home/<user>`
  paths in the script or in journal `source` strings (check-agnostic.sh).
